findings.body:
**Parse only stdout in `gitLsRemoteRef`. Do not parse stdout and stderr together.**

Line 819 joins stdout and stderr without a separator, and Lines 826-833 parse that combined text as the ref listing. Git can write warnings to stderr when the command succeeds. One example is `warning: redirecting to ...` for a renamed GitHub repo. Two failures follow:

- If the ref exists, stdout ends in `\n` and stderr is appended after it. Line 827 then throws "matched multiple refs".
- If the ref is absent, stdout is empty but `output` is not. Line 826 does not return `null`, and Line 831 throws "returned no commit oid".

The gate fails closed in both cases, but it refuses for a false reason. Parse the redacted stdout, and use the combined text only in error messages.

<details>
<summary>Proposed fix</summary>

```diff
-  const output = redactSecrets(`${res.stdout.toString('utf8')}${res.stderr}`.trim(), secrets);
+  const listing = redactSecrets(res.stdout.toString('utf8').trim(), secrets);
+  const output = redactSecrets(`${res.stdout.toString('utf8')}\n${res.stderr}`.trim(), secrets);
   if (res.timedOut) {
     throw new Error(`ratchet git: ls-remote timed out after ${EXEC_TIMEOUT_MS}ms`);
   }
-  if (!res.ok || res.code !== 0) {
+  if (!res.ok) {
     throw new Error(`ratchet git: ls-remote failed: ${output || `exit ${String(res.code)}`}`);
   }
-  if (output === '') return null;
-  if (output.includes('\n')) {
+  if (listing === '') return null;
+  if (listing.includes('\n')) {
     throw new Error(`ratchet git: ls-remote matched multiple refs for '${ref}'`);
   }
-  const oid = output.split('\t', 1)[0] ?? '';
+  const oid = listing.split('\t', 1)[0] ?? '';
   if (!OID.test(oid)) {
-    throw new Error(`ratchet git: ls-remote returned no commit oid ('${output}')`);
+    throw new Error(`ratchet git: ls-remote returned no commit oid ('${listing}')`);
   }
```
</details>
